## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design secure cross-account workflows using ABAC, STS, KMS, and tenant isolation. It emphasizes least privilege, tenant isolation, and compliance requirements—critical skills for building enterprise-grade data pipelines.

## Key Concepts

- **IAM tag-based access control (ABAC)** – Use tags to grant access based on attributes
- **STS AssumeRole with session tags** – Pass tenant-id via aws:PrincipalTag and aws:SessionTag for attribute-based authorization
- **KMS key policy** – Condition access on matching session/principal tags
- **S3 bucket policy** – Enforce TLS-only, SSE-KMS, and no public access
- **Cognito JWT validation** – Authenticate device requests

## Trust Policy (Processing Lambda Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "Service": "lambda.amazonaws.com"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:SourceAccount": "123456789012"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Permission Policy (Processing Lambda Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::*:role/TenantRole*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        },
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Trust Policy (Compliance Tenant Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/ProcessingLambdaRole"
      },
      "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "sts:ExternalId": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}",
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Permission Policy (Compliance Tenant Role)

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": "s3:PutObject",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/data/${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "aws:kms",
          "aws:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## KMS Key Policy

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Principal": {
        "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::*:role/TenantRole*"
      },
      "Action": "kms:Encrypt",
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "kms:RequestTag/tenant-id": "${aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id}"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## S3 Bucket Policy

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {
          "aws:SecureTransport": "false"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Principal": "*",
      "Action": "s3:*",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::compliance-bucket/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:PublicAccess": "true"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

## Test Plan

| Test Case | Description | Expected Result |
|-----------|-------------|------------------|
| **1. Valid JWT with tenant-a** | Send request with valid Cognito JWT for tenant-a | Lambda assumes TenantRole-a, writes to tenant-a/ partition |
| **2. Invalid JWT** | Send request with expired/invalid JWT | API Gateway rejects with 401 Unauthorized |
| **3. Cross-tenant access attempt** | Lambda for tenant-a attempts to write to tenant-b path | Access denied - principal tag mismatch |
| **4. Non-TLS connection** | Attempt PUT over HTTP | S3 bucket policy denies request |
| **5. KMS key access by untagged role** | Role without tenant-id tag attempts encryption | KMS policy denies encryption |
| **6. Public access attempt** | Attempt to access bucket publicly | Bucket policy denies - no public access enforced |
| **7. Session tag verification** | Verify STS passes tenant-id as session tag | CloudTrail shows aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id matches aws:SessionTag/tenant-id |
| **8. Parquet file verification** | Write and read back Parquet files | Files correctly partitioned by date and tenant |

## Why This Is Asked

This validates practical isolation in a shared data lake, ensuring least privilege and scalable onboarding. It also tests policy layering and auditing capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- IAM roles per tenant with strict resource boundaries
- Trust policies tied to the tenant app identity
- S3 prefix-scoped permissions with bucket or IAM policy conditions
- Onboarding automation for new tenants and centralized governance
- Cross-tenant test plans and auditing hooks

## Code Example

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake",
      "Condition": {"StringLike": {"s3:prefix": "tenant-<tid>/*"}}
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["s3:GetObject","s3:PutObject"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::corp-data-lake/tenant-<tid>/*",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": ["sts:AssumeRole"],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:iam::<account>:role/TenantRole-<tid>",
      "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"aws:PrincipalTag/tenant-id": "<tid>"}}
    }
  ]
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you extend this model to support cross-region backups without cross-tenant data leakage?
- How would you automate onboarding for new tenants without touching code (CI/CD policy issuance, audit log integration)?

